.TH BIOSEQ.FASTA 4 2000-1月 "open.fasta" "open.fasta"
.SH NAME
open.fasta \- open the fasta sequence file
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fIopen.fasta(\fBfile\fR as string, 
\fBread\fR as boolean = TRUE, 
\fBline_break\fR as integer = -1, 
\fBdelimiter\fR as string = "|", 
[\fB<Environment>\fR]);\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
open the fasta sequence file
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fBfile\fB \fR\- 
 the file path of the target fasta sequence file for open.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBread\fB \fR\- 
 load a set of fasta sequence data in lazy mode? default is yes.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBline_break\fB \fR\- 
 the sequence length in one line of the generated fasta document when this 
 function is used for open a fasta file in write mode, a negative value 
 means that all of the sequence data will be written in a single line.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBdelimiter\fB \fR\- 
 the delimiter character for merge the fasta headers title when this 
 function is used for open a fasta file in write mode.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBenv\fB \fR\- the R# runtime environment object.. 
.PP
.SH VALUE
.PP
a lazy collection of the fasta sequence data(a pipeline object of the 
 @\fBT:SMRUCC.genomics.SequenceModel.FASTA.FastaSeq\fR sequence data) when the \fBread\fR parameter is TRUE, 
 or a fasta stream writer(@\fBT:SMRUCC.genomics.SequenceModel.FASTA.StreamWriter\fR) 
 object for write the sequence data into the target file in a stream manner 
 when the \fBread\fR parameter is FALSE.
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
bioseq.fasta
.SH FILES
.PP
seqtoolkit.dll
.PP
